{
  "id": "ss.char.cap",
  "name": "Cap",
  "description": "A survivor of the same brood as everything hunting you — same feelers, same organ, same socket in the shell. The organ is `dead`: no halo, no bloom, a hairline crack across cold grey, and that silence is the premise all eight wear in the same place. The plated box, unchanged, rivets and all — with a fungus cap set on top of it and two spores coming off the back. A fungus beetle that never left the fruiting body it hatched in, so the cap is worn rather than grown, and it is the armour the stat line is paying for. The feelers swing out from under the brim instead of up through it, which is the only concession the shell makes.",
  "tags": ["ss-char"],
  "size": [36, 36],
  "meta": { "radius": 12 },
  "parts": [
    { "id": "antenna_far", "use": "ss.lib.antenna", "variant": "dead", "at": [7.2, -10.4], "rot": -14, "scale": 0.5 },
